<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Twenty-eighth Dynasty of Egypt</h1><p class="st-meta">404 BCE – 398 BCE · capital Sais</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A one-king dynasty under Amyrtaeus of Sais, who freed Egypt from Persian rule in 404 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amyrtaeus">Amyrtaeus</a>, a prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sais">Sais</a> and probably a grandson of an earlier rebel of the same name, led a revolt against <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/achaemenid-egypt">Achaemenid Egypt</a> when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-ii">Darius II</a> died in 404 BCE. By about 400 BCE even the Jewish garrison at Elephantine dated its documents by his reign.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Very little is known of his rule. He controlled the Delta and gradually the whole country, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, distracted by the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-younger">Cyrus the Younger</a>, did not try to recover <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 399 to 398 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amyrtaeus">Amyrtaeus</a> was overthrown by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepherites-i">Nepherites I</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mendes">Mendes</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/twenty-ninth-dynasty-of-egypt">Twenty-ninth Dynasty of Egypt</a>; an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aramaic">Aramaic</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papyrus">papyrus</a> suggests he was executed.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 404 BCE – 398 BCE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:51.66%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>404 BCE – 398 BCE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sais</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Amyrtaeus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Egyptian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Egyptian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Twenty-eighth Dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-401&amp;focus=twenty-eighth-dynasty-of-egypt" aria-label="Twenty-eighth Dynasty of Egypt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5476 1049 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Twenty-eighth Dynasty of Egypt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5796 1305L5813 1344M5796 1305L5815 1305"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5813 1344h0M5815 1305h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5796 1305h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5796 1305h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Sais. <a href="/atlas?year=-401&amp;focus=twenty-eighth-dynasty-of-egypt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
